@startuml
title Vina Bim Shop Section 01 Lambda Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 180

actor "Executive Teams\n1-hour freshness" as Executive
actor "BI/Livestreaming Teams\nreal-time visibility" as BI

rectangle "Source Systems" as Sources {
  component "Offline source snapshots\ncustomers, sellers, products,\norders, payments, shipments" as Offline
  component "JSON event producer\nhuman-readable payloads" as Producer
}

queue "Kafka\ncommerce_events\ncatalog_events\nfulfillment_events\nops_events" as Kafka

rectangle "Lambda Processing Paths" as Lambda {
  component "Spark Batch Path\nhourly validation, dedup,\nschema evolution handling,\nbatch aggregates" as Spark
  component "Flink Streaming Path\nevent-time watermarks,\nallowed lateness,\nreal-time revenue/issues/anomalies" as Flink
}

database "MinIO Medallion Lakehouse\nBronze raw JSON/Parquet\nSilver cleaned standard records\nGold deferred to Section 02" as MinIO
database "Hive Metastore\nlakehouse table metadata" as Hive
component "Trino\nSQL query access" as Trino

Offline --> MinIO : raw Parquet snapshots
Producer --> Kafka : JSON envelope events
Kafka --> Flink : direct stream consumption
Kafka --> MinIO : replayable Bronze JSON
MinIO --> Spark : hourly batch inputs
Spark --> MinIO : Silver and later Gold outputs
Flink --> MinIO : real-time Bronze/Silver-ready outputs
MinIO --> Hive : table registration
Hive --> Trino : catalog metadata
Trino --> Executive : hourly BI extracts
Flink --> BI : seconds-level operational views
Trino --> BI : SQL exploration and reconciled views

note bottom of MinIO
Section 01 owns source simulation, raw contracts, event topics, and evidence.
Section 02 owns runnable Spark/Flink jobs and final Gold schema design.
end note

@enduml
